{
  "id": "u04-l02",
  "unit": "u04-food",
  "title": "Drinks",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "**পানি** (*pani*) is water in Bangladesh. In Kolkata — and among many Hindus in Bangladesh — it's **জল** (*jol*). The choice can signal community, so just follow what the people around you say.\n\n**চা** (*cha*) is everywhere: tiny roadside stalls serve **দুধ চা** (milk tea), often very sweet, or **রং চা** (red tea, no milk). **এক কাপ চা** = 'one cup tea' — no word for 'of'.\n\n**ছাড়া** (*chhara*) 'without' is a postposition, so it comes **after**: **চিনি ছাড়া** = 'without sugar'. Handy at a tea stall, because sugar is the default!\n\n**লবণ কোথায়?** 'Where's the salt?' — and **চিনি নেই** 'There's no sugar.'",
